  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Noor Rauf Shaikh vs The State Of Maharashtra on 10 January, 2020 Author: R. G. Avachat Bench: R. G. Avachat 1 aba-1563-19.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1563 Of 2019 Noor Rauf Shaikh ... Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra and another ... Respondents .... Mr. Akram Inamdar, Advocate h/f Mr. Y. B. Pathan, Advocate for applicant. Mr. R. V. Dasalkar, App for respondents-State. .... Coram : R. G. Avachat, J. Dated : 10th January, 2020 Per Court :- . This is an application for bail under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure.",
    "facts": "The applicant claims to have an apprehension of being arrested in connection with Crime No.0118/2019, registered at Sonai Police Station, Tq. Newasa, Dist. Ahmednagar, for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 of the Indian Penal Code and under Section 59 read with Sections 3.1.7 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Noor Rauf Shaikh vs The State Of Maharashtra on 10 January, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/134917940/ 1 1 of 3 ::: Uploaded on - 16/01/2020 ::: Downloaded on - 08/06/2020 17:47:33 :: 2 aba-1563-19.doc 2. Perused the First Information Report (FIR) and related papers. FIR has been lodged by the Food Safety Officer on 28.03.2019. It is alleged in the FIR that a vehicle - Maruti Suzuki Omni MH-17 AJ-1182, was intercepted at Pandhricha Pul. Govind Loya was in the driver seat. On search of the vehicle, it was found to have contained contraband food articles, namely, 208 packets of Hira Pan Masala, 208 packets of Royal Tobacco and 51 packets of Goa Gutkha. Those articles came to be seized under the panchnama. The applicant claims to have apprehension of arrest, since, accused Govind Loya seems to have informed the police that he had purchased those food articles from the applicant and others. 3. I have observed that Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code is not applicable in case of storing, sale or transporting contraband articles, namely, Gutkha, Pan Masala, Tobacco etc. Rest of the offences are bailable one. Except the statement of co-accused, there is nothing to indicate the applicant's involvement in the alleged offence. Contraband articles have been seized on the spot.",
